IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp6-administration`

-- Tests of cp6-administration.l4 (sections 92 to 94, lines 2638 to 2651 of the Act file).

§ `Tests -- administration of the Act`

§§ `Section 92(1) and (2): which Minister has control and direction`

#ASSERT `s 92 — the Minister with control and direction of the administration of the part` `Part I of the Act` EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`
#ASSERT `s 92 — the Minister with control and direction of the administration of the part` `a Part of the Act other than Part I` EQUALS `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`

§§ `Section 92(2): what the Minister of National Revenue must report`

-- Inputs: the kind of information; obtained under this Act; the Minister requires it for the purpose the paragraph describes; necessary for the administration of the Act.
-- (a) and (b) need the information to have been obtained under the Act and required by the Minister.
#ASSERT `s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `earnings information needed to determine a benefit or a financial adjustment` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `earnings information needed to determine a benefit or a financial adjustment` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c) needs only that the information is necessary for the administration of the Act.
#ASSERT `s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Information of another kind is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `information of another kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Section 92(3): a report for policy analysis, research or evaluation`

#ASSERT `s 92(3) — the report may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(3) — the report may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92(3) — the report may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Sections 93 and 94: assistance as the Governor in Council directs`

#ASSERT `s 93 — the Minister of Public Works and Government Services must furnish the Minister with the assistance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93 — the Minister of Public Works and Government Services must furnish the Minister with the assistance` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 94 — the Canada Employment Insurance Commission must furnish the Minister and the Minister of National Revenue with the assistance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 94 — the Canada Employment Insurance Commission must furnish the Minister and the Minister of National Revenue with the assistance` FALSE)
